---
description: Flask routes rules (thin controllers, secure endpoints)
globs:
  - "Server/app/routes/**"
alwaysApply: false
---
# Routes
- Keep routes thin; delegate business logic to `app/services`.
- Validate requests using shared validators/decorators in `app/utils`.
- Enforce auth and role checks consistently; verify JWTs and permissions.
- Return standardized error shapes; avoid leaking internals.
- Respect CORS and security headers; no ad-hoc overrides.
